  m_text: "Spline Extrude can also sweep a square profile to make a curb, a low wall or a beam. The mesh is rebuilt each time the spline changes, so one curb follows any edge of a plaza, straight or curved.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> You move one knot of the curb's spline 2 m outward. What happens to the curb?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select Curb, switch to the Spline context and move a knot 2 m outward.\n2. Under Geometry, set Radius to 0.3.\n3. Under Shape Extrude, set Type to Circle, then back to Square, and compare.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Mesh-Shape 6 \xB7 Floor plans with Poly Shape</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
