  m_text: "The Spline Extrude component builds a mesh along a spline by sweeping a profile along it. With a circle profile it makes a tube: a railing, a pipe, a cable. Radius sets its thickness; Sides sets how many flat faces go around it.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> You lower Sides from 12 to 4. What will the railing look like?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select Railing. In Spline Extrude, under Shape Extrude, set Sides to 4.\n2. Under Geometry, set Radius to 0.1.\n3. Switch to the Spline context, drag a knot and watch the mesh follow.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Liminal-Kit 2 \xB7 Levels (Stairs)</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
